RT and non-RT scheduling policies:
	SCHED_DEADLINE > SCHED_RR/SCHED_FIFO > SCHED_OTHER > SCHED_BATCH > SCHED_IDLE
	|---------- RT --------------------|   |-------------- non-RT --------------|

Priorities:
	<---------------------------------------------------------------------------|High priority
					     |---------	Nice -----------------------|			
					      -20				   +19
	|				     |					    |
	0				   99 100				   139
	|<-	rt_prio			   ->|<- 	static_prio		  ->|				
    prio|--------------------------------------------------------------------------->	
VxWorks
	|				     |
	255				     0
Types of priorities:
	1. static_prio
		- non RT
		- static_prio = 120 + nice
	2. rt_prio
		- RT
		- MAX_RT_PRIO-1 - rt_priority
	3. normal_prio
		- RT		= MAX_RT_PRIO-1 - rt_priority	
		- non RT	= static_prio
	4. prio
		- effective priority [ boosting priority, mapping priorities for all the scheduling policies]
		- RT : MAX_RT_PRIORITY - 1 - rt_priority

To check priorities in procfs:
	/proc/<pid>/stat
		- cat /proc/<pid>/stat | awk '{ print $18 "," $40 }'
							|	|--- rt_prio[real time priority only applicable for RT task]
							|----------- [top output show this value][also ps -o priority ][prio - MAX_RT_PRIO]
	/proc/<pid>/sched

Change priority:
	- RT		: chrt -p <prio> <pid>
	- non RT	: renice -n <prio> -p <pid>

	
	

